  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 18,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/79eee82dc831e25c4ecb7bd46a8c7c48f96622e9/docs%2Ffeatures%2Fbatch_invariance.md",
      "changes": 18,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/docs%2Ffeatures%2Fbatch_invariance.md?ref=79eee82dc831e25c4ecb7bd46a8c7c48f96622e9",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/features/batch_invariance.md",
      "patch": "@@ -161,6 +161,24 @@ When batch invariance is enabled, vLLM:\n !!! note\n     Enabling batch invariance may impact performance compared to the default non-deterministic mode. This trade-off is intentional to guarantee reproducibility.\n \n+### NVLS and fixed-batch reproducibility\n+\n+On Hopper NVSwitch nodes (H100, H20, H800), the dominant source of\n+run-to-run non-determinism for a single request is NVLS all-reduce (in-switch\n+reduction of large prefill all-reduces). This is fixed by `NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0`,\n+which is one of the many NCCL settings applied by batch invariance.\n+\n+If you only need **fixed-batch reproducibility** (the same request always\n+produces the same output) rather than full batch invariance (outputs\n+independent of batch composition), setting `NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0` alone is\n+sufficient and costs only ~1% latency — compared to ~76% for the full\n+batch-invariance NCCL overrides. See\n+[Reproducibility](../usage/reproducibility.md#nvswitch-nvls-non-determinism-on-hopper)\n+for details.\n+\n+Note that the NVLS fix requires kernel driver / Fabric Manager ≥ 550.144.03 (or\n+570+); upgrading CUDA/NCCL alone does not help.\n+\n ## Future Improvements\n \n The batch invariance feature is under active development. Planned improvements include:",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/79eee82dc831e25c4ecb7bd46a8c7c48f96622e9/docs%2Ffeatures%2Fbatch_invariance.md",
      "sha": "83a7304846af500d7c0a6a00c6bc68ee2add7716",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 21,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/79eee82dc831e25c4ecb7bd46a8c7c48f96622e9/docs%2Fusage%2Freproducibility.md",
      "changes": 21,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/docs%2Fusage%2Freproducibility.md?ref=79eee82dc831e25c4ecb7bd46a8c7c48f96622e9",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/usage/reproducibility.md",
      "patch": "@@ -19,6 +19,27 @@ Example: [examples/features/batch_invariance/reproducibility_offline.py](../../e\n     Even with the above settings, vLLM only provides reproducibility\n     when it runs on the same hardware and the same vLLM version.\n \n+## NVSwitch (NVLS) non-determinism on Hopper\n+\n+On Hopper nodes with NVSwitch (e.g. H100, H20, H800), NVLS all-reduce results\n+can differ between runs when the kernel driver or Fabric Manager is older than\n+550.144.03 (or 570+). This causes run-to-run output differences even for a\n+single request on an otherwise idle server. Upgrading CUDA or NCCL alone does\n+**not** fix this — the fix is in the kernel driver / Fabric Manager (see\n+[NCCL#2360](https://github.com/NVIDIA/nccl/issues/2360)).\n+\n+If you only need the same request to produce the same output (fixed-batch\n+reproducibility) and do not need full batch invariance, you can set\n+`NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0` instead of enabling the full batch-invariance mode. This\n+resolves NVLS-induced divergence with approximately 1% latency overhead,\n+compared to ~76% for the full set of batch-invariance NCCL overrides.\n+\n+| Setting | Divergence | Latency cost |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| default | ~25% of reruns diverge | 1× |\n+| `NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0` | 0% | ~1.01× |\n+| Full batch invariance (`VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1`) | 0% | ~1.76× |\n+\n ## Setting the global seed\n \n The `seed` parameter in vLLM is used to control the random states for various random number generators.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/79eee82dc831e25c4ecb7bd46a8c7c48f96622e9/docs%2Fusage%2Freproducibility.md",
      "sha": "853951eecf866b247ae30bb2ca6d46e8d18e43e0",
      "status": "modified"
    }
